  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nThe low is forecast to move into New Mexico by Wednesday morning \nand well into the Plains by Thursday with dry air advection and \nsubsidence increasing across our area. Generally clear skies are \nexpected for the lower deserts on Wednesday and eventually over \neastern Arizona by later the afternoon. Fairly strong ridging is \nthen forecast to move into the region on Thursday with H5 heights \nquickly rising to between 586-590dm. Despite the quick boost in \nheights aloft, temperatures will be somewhat slow to recover, \nespecially over the eastern half of Arizona. Highs should stay \nbelow 90 degrees in the Phoenix area through Thursday with the \nlower deserts warming back into the mid to upper 90s. As the \nboundary layer gradually dries out going into the weekend, we are \nlikely to return to our typically lower humidity levels while \ntemperatures warm to slightly above normal.",
